TakesScreenShot<I> 

-> its an interface which consist of one abstract method which is getScreenshotAs()
-> To access this method we should do downcasting from webdriver to TakesScreenShot

why?
-> Whenever there is diffrence between expected result and actual result
-> To drop it in the bug / defect report

ways?

-> 2 ways

1. Screenshot of a webpage
2. screenshot of an element

// Mouse Actions 

1. mouse hover -> moveToElement()
2. drag and drop
3. click 
4. right click
5. double click
6. scroll

Actions --> concrete class 

syntax -> Actions act = new Actions(browser address);

How to perform mouse actions 

-> We need to create an object of actions class and we need to pass the driver as an argument
-> Actions act = new Actions(driver);

-> use reference varibale and access the methods


